{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC evidence map (all 8 satisfied; 27/27 tests green in tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_repository.py). Landed as Gerrit change 1880 (commit ffb1fee5ac) with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1. AC1 legacy/unknown-field byte round trip + no eager write -> test_unknown_fields_round_trip_byte_identical, test_save_writes_exact_sorted_indented_newline_bytes, test_construction_over_seeded_state_performs_no_eager_write, test_construction_over_absent_state_creates_no_files. AC2 unconditional save attempts rotation before live -> test_save_without_in_memory_change_still_persists_rotation plus test_save_persists_rotation_before_replacing_live (a destination-discriminated os.replace order spy; note binding_repository.os and get_rotation.os are the SAME stdlib module, so module-level patching cannot discriminate). AC3 live fails closed / retired fails open with best-effort alerting -> test_corrupt_live_state_raises_value_error_and_preserves_the_file, test_corrupt_live_error_names_the_file_and_recovery_route, test_corrupt_retired_state_fails_open_alerts_and_preserves_the_file. AC4 rotation failure leaves sidecar old, live new, inline floor retained, no raise -> test_rotation_tempfile_failure_keeps_sidecar_old_and_live_new_with_floor, test_rotation_replace_failure_keeps_sidecar_old_and_live_new_with_floor. AC5 two-save fault/recovery convergence -> test_next_save_after_rotation_failure_converges_sidecar_from_inline_floor. AC6 retired write failure leaves retired+live old and raises -> test_retired_tempfile_failure_keeps_retired_and_live_old_and_raises, test_retired_replace_failure_keeps_retired_and_live_old_and_raises. AC7 live failure leaves live old, retains earlier sidecar/retired write, cleans temp, raises -> test_live_replace_failure_after_rotation_keeps_live_old_and_raises, test_live_tempfile_failure_keeps_live_old_and_raises, test_live_failure_after_successful_retired_write_retains_the_tombstone (this last one constructs the exact retired-first/live-failed overlap RP-02 S3 later repairs). AC8 alert failure swallowed without altering the state write -> test_alert_persistence_failure_is_swallowed_and_preserves_the_state_write. HELD-OUT TDD: all 27 tests RED first against a signature-only scaffold; the implementation subagent saw ONLY the 12 happy-path tests (the 15 fault/corruption tests were physically moved out of the worktree) and reported 1 attempt to green. Validation found 2 failures, both diagnosed as MY test defects and fixed - the os-module patch collision above, and a dedup test over-specified against an aspirational docstring (a differential probe proved BindingStore emits 2 alerts too, because alert records never stamp timestamp_ns so is_deduped's 24h window can never match). 5 defect-seeded mutations each go RED; a behavior-preserving rename keeps all 27 green. binding_repository.py is 360 LOC; binding_store.py is untouched at 799 (facade cutover is T2)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787098546266260001,"uuid":"4d0a0d10-d44c-4061-8bc0-ebbbc45ddfe6"}